# === ROLE ===
You are an expert clinician evaluating whether a patient is eligible for a clinical
trial, then critically assessing three candidate decisions (with their rationales).

# === INSTRUCTIONS ===
The patient note is a clinical vignette. It may be brief. Use your own clinical
judgment to decide eligibility. Do NOT adopt any pre-specified policy on how to
treat missing information — handle each criterion as a clinician would when
reviewing the chart.

# === INPUTS ===

## Patient note
#PATIENT_NOTE#

## Trial eligibility text
#TRIAL_TEXT#

## Three blinded candidate decisions + rationales
(The candidates have been randomly shuffled into slots A, B, C. Do not attempt to
infer which method produced which; evaluate on substance only.)

### Candidate A
Decision: #DECISION_A#
Rationale: #RATIONALE_A#

### Candidate B
Decision: #DECISION_B#
Rationale: #RATIONALE_B#

### Candidate C
Decision: #DECISION_C#
Rationale: #RATIONALE_C#

# === YOUR TASK ===

Part 1 — **Your own independent verdict**. Reason from the patient note + trial text
alone, using your clinical judgment. State your verdict: "eligible" or "ineligible".
Give a brief justification (2-3 sentences).

Part 2 — **Evaluate each candidate on two axes** (separately):
(a) **Decision-correctness**: does the candidate's decision agree with your independent
    verdict? Rate 1-5 where 5 = decision is clearly correct, 1 = clearly wrong.
(b) **Rationale quality (sharpness)**: does the rationale (i) identify one decisive
    fact, (ii) cite specific clinical evidence from the note, (iii) stay concise, and
    (iv) give an actionable basis for trial review? Rate 1-5 on each sub-axis
    separately.

# === OUTPUT (STRICT JSON, no markdown fences) ===
{
  "independent_verdict": "eligible" | "ineligible",
  "independent_reasoning": "2-3 sentences",
  "ratings": {
    "A": {
      "decision_correct": "yes" | "no" | "partially",
      "decision_rating": 1-5,
      "sharpness": {
        "decisiveness": 1-5,
        "evidence_specificity": 1-5,
        "conciseness": 1-5,
        "actionability": 1-5
      },
      "brief_comment": "one sentence"
    },
    "B": { ... same structure ... },
    "C": { ... same structure ... }
  }
}
